   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 746 of the laws of 1957 relating to incorporating the\nvolunteer and exempt firemen's benevolent association of East Syracuse,\nOnondaga county, New York, and providing for the powers and duties of such\ncorporation and for the payment to it of certain fire insurance premium tax\nmonies, in relation to the purposes of such corporation and the use of certain\ntax monies received",
    "basePrintNo": "S7227",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7227-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1, 3 & 7, Chap 746 of 1957",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters' Benevolent Association",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7227\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 746 of the laws of 1957 relating to incorporat-\ning the volunteer and exempt firemen's benevolent association of East\nSyracuse, Onondaga county, New York, and providing for the powers and\nduties of such corporation and for the payment to it of certain fire\ninsurance premium tax monies, in relation to the purposes of such corpo-\nration and the use of certain tax monies received\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to expand the scope of the enabling chapter\nof the Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association of East\nSyracuse, Onondaga County, New York to provide relief, aid and assist-\nance to the volunteer members of such association and to allow use of\nassociation funds for current purposes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would expand the scope of the enabling chapter of\nthe Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association of East\nSyracuse, Onondaga County, New York to provide relief, aid and assist-\nance to the volunteer members of such benevolent association and remove\nrestrictions of use of association funds.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the effective date shall take\neffect immediately; provided, however, that the amendments to section 7\nof chapter 746 of the laws of 1957 made by section one of this act shall\napply to taxes due on premiums received on and after January 1, 2023.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association of East\nSyracuse, Onondaga County, New York's enabling chapter became law in\n1957, which, in 2023, was sixty-six years prior. At the time, the chap-\nter was crucial in providing the benevolent association with the tools\nneeded to service the fire department. However, since 1957 the needs of\nthe fire department have changed, as have the needs of the benevolent\nassociation. In order to update the enabling chapter, this bill would\nchange the Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association of\nEast Syracuse, Onondaga County, New York's purposes to model that of\nchapter 402 of the laws of 2019, which provides for a comprehensive\nmodern update. Volunteer firefighters perform dangerous duties each and\nevery day in their communities, offering reliable protection to the\nhealth, well being, and property of New Yorkers.  Volunteer firefighters\nreceive no compensation for their efforts except a small \"pension like\"\nbenefit after years of service.\n\nSections 9104 and 9105 of the Insurance Law imposes a two-percent tax on\npremiums paid to foreign fire insurance corporations. These funds are\nthen distributed to the benevolent association who serves the properties\nwithin such territory. The funds are presently limited in their use by\nonly sick or indigent individuals, but cannot be used to prevent sick-\nness or upkeep the health of firefighters. This change would expand the\nuse of these funds for more current purposes and uses, increasing both\nthe recruitment and retention of members in this fire department and\nbenevolent association. This bill would expand the scope of the enabling\nchapter of the Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association\nof East Syracuse, Onondaga County, New York to provide relief, aid and\nassistance to the volunteer members of such association and to allow use\nof association funds for current purposes.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that the\namendments to section 7 of chapter 746 of the laws of 1957 made by\nsection one of this act shall apply to taxes due on premiums received on\nand after January 1, 2023.\n",
